-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Schedule II (Section 190), paragraph 18: the table of weeks of benefit
-- that applies in place of Schedule I from June 30, 1996 until Schedule I comes into force on January 5, 1997 (s 190(4)).
-- Written by piece ei6 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24; the rows below were generated by a script that reads the raw file
-- (src:3386-3426), so no figure is typed by hand. Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws
-- consolidation current to 2026-09-30; nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- The rows are the number of weeks of insurable employment (12 to 52); the columns are the same twelve bands of the
-- regional rate of unemployment as in Schedule I. A blank cell is NOTHING. A number of weeks that is not a whole number
-- from 12 to 52 has no row, so it is NOTHING too (the text gives none; fork F-ei6-8 in NOTES.md).
--
-- The interim Schedule I is named "Schedule II para 18 ..." so that it cannot clash with the rule of piece ei1 for
-- the hours-based Schedule I, which this piece also encodes as "Act Schedule I ...".

§ `Schedule II, paragraph 18 - Schedule I, Table of Weeks of Benefit`

